WEBVTT

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:45.540
Way to go, Miyazaki!

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:49.290
Geez, we're not lucky.

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:52.320
The artificial turf is making it harder to pitch and easier to slip on your feet.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:54.950
It's gotten difficult to run without slipping.

00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:56.250
It's not luck.

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:00.430
Shigeno is using this rain.

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:03.890
Batting eighth: center fielder, Takahashi-kun.

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:06.640
All right! Keep it going, Takahashi!

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:09.990
Strike! Batter out!

00:02:09.990 --> 00:02:11.470
Three outs! Change!

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:13.390
Don't mind, don't mind!

00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:15.120
Things are flowing our way!

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:16.410
Let's shut them down!

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:17.650
YEAH!

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:19.530
Ichihara.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:23.750
If you allow any more runs, I'll take you off the mound immediately.

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:28.360
You'll lose your guarantee to stand on the mound for Koshien as well.

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:30.140
Bear that in mind.

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:31.640
Y-Yes, sir.

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:35.830
Play!

00:02:44.590 --> 00:02:46.430
Strike! Batter out!

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:48.150
Three outs! Change!

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:53.900
<i>I had a loose ball in this inning too, but...</i>

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:57.190
<i>They all saw them as balls and didn't swing.</i>

00:02:57.190 --> 00:03:00.150
<i>It really seems like the ones aiming for them are...</i>

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:05.620
<i>This isn't a joke!</i>

00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:10.470
<i>I've done my best for three years, and to be thrown aside due to something tiny like this...</i>

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:12.580
<i>How can I go back to the bench after all this?</i>

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:24.450
Strike! Batter out!

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:27.770
Looks like your threat worked.

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:29.290
"Threat"?

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:33.690
Batting first: right fielder, Shimizu-kun.

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:39.330
I thought Ichihara-kun was breaking down,
but it looks like he's somehow brought himself back.

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:40.150
Yeah.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:43.810
But this batter got a hit earlier today, so...

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:50.960
Strike!

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:55.660
<i>A forkball on the first pitch?</i>

00:03:56.010 --> 00:03:59.680
<i>They're really trying to push back Taiga, since he's gotten two hits.</i>

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:03.830
Strike!

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:11.220
Ball!

00:04:11.610 --> 00:04:13.180
Taiga, hit it!

00:04:14.010 --> 00:04:18.320
<i>If this inning ends with just those three, Ichihara will be back on his feet!</i>

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:19.900
<i>Come on, Taiga!</i>

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:22.430
<i>I won't let you...</i>

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:24.690
<i>get any more hits!</i>

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:30.370
All right!

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:36.080
Awesome, Shimizu-san!

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:38.860
Your younger brother has gotten three hits in three at-bats!

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:42.540
And he hit the opponent's decisive forkball!

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:45.780
Well, he's trained under his older sister's strict tutelage, after all.

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:47.480
I-Is that so...

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:50.910
Akutsu, get warmed up.

00:04:50.910 --> 00:04:51.680
Right.

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:58.270
<i>Akutsu's heading towards the bullpen...</i>

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:02.060
Batting second: third baseman, Uchiyama-kun.

00:05:02.390 --> 00:05:06.190
Come on! Send it flying, Uchiyama!

00:05:06.190 --> 00:05:07.530
<i>Or just, say...</i>

00:05:15.490 --> 00:05:16.960
To first!

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:18.250
Out!

00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:19.630
Yeah!

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:21.210
Uchiyama, nice bunt!

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:26.690
Batting third: pitcher, Shigeno-kun.

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:33.340
<i>I'll definitely hit it.</i>

00:05:33.340 --> 00:05:36.650
<i>If we can score a run this inning, the flow will be going our way!</i>

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:38.610
Play!

00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:42.320
<i>Do you think...</i>

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:45.320
<i>I'll stand for becoming a bench warmer after coming all the way here!?</i>

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:47.530
Ball!

00:05:50.060 --> 00:05:50.920
Ball!

00:05:50.920 --> 00:05:51.820
Ball two!

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:53.670
You bastard!

00:05:53.670 --> 00:05:57.090
Are you really going to walk me because you're scared!?

00:05:57.460 --> 00:05:58.270
Time.

00:06:00.110 --> 00:06:01.690
What are you running away from?

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:02.880
Face him.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:05.250
If we get another runner on base, the risks will increase.

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:07.130
Y-Yeah.

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:08.720
I'm trying to, but...

00:06:11.090 --> 00:06:12.070
I see.

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:14.470
You don't want to let them score any more runs either.

00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:18.680
You're concerned with what Egashira-san said to you, right?

00:06:18.680 --> 00:06:20.440
N-No.

00:06:20.830 --> 00:06:22.940
Then make it clear and walk him.

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:25.900
Being wishy-washy about it would be the worst.

00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:29.540
It's not a situation where we can be certain that we'll hold them back completely,

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:32.910
but the pitcher doesn't have to give a challenge when he doesn't want to.

00:06:33.470 --> 00:06:34.420
Sato...

00:06:36.290 --> 00:06:39.630
Instead, make sure you bring down the next guy, Tashiro.

00:06:40.270 --> 00:06:43.830
It's all right. Your pitches don't get hit easily.

00:06:46.070 --> 00:06:49.960
I'm sure you told him to face me, right?

00:06:51.460 --> 00:06:52.600
HEY!

00:06:54.130 --> 00:06:54.980
Ball!

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:56.260
Four balls!

00:06:56.260 --> 00:06:58.560
Damn it, I'll remember this!

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:04.850
Batting fourth: catcher, Tashiro-kun.

00:07:04.850 --> 00:07:06.650
<i>I'm counting on you, Tashiro!</i>

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:07.830
Play!

00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:11.380
<i>They won't want to load the bases,</i>

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:14.570
<i>so they'll try to bring me down quickly for sure.</i>

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:18.570
<i>But, I can't expect to get a fastball that's easy to hit.</i>

00:07:19.030 --> 00:07:23.040
<i>He'll throw the breaking ball that's been hit the least.</i>

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:24.290
<i>That's...</i>

00:07:24.690 --> 00:07:26.890
<i>The one that doesn't even match Katori's sharpness...</i>

00:07:26.890 --> 00:07:28.800
<i>an outside slider!</i>

00:07:34.540 --> 00:07:36.260
S-Safe! Safe!

00:07:37.420 --> 00:07:39.280
Run, Taiga!

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:41.770
Izumi, get it!

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:46.690
Izumi!

00:07:46.690 --> 00:07:47.440
Safe!

00:07:56.510 --> 00:07:58.520
Sorry, that was a godsend.

00:07:58.520 --> 00:08:00.370
Safe! Safe!

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:03.100
All right!

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:05.210
We got two runs back!

00:08:06.900 --> 00:08:11.720
Hey, hey, if the runner is hit with the ball, isn't he out?

00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:16.370
Before that, the third baseman's glove touched the ball, right?

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:19.110
T-That's true.

00:08:24.030 --> 00:08:25.470
<i>Luck?</i>

00:08:25.470 --> 00:08:27.810
<i>No, it's not just that.</i>

00:08:27.810 --> 00:08:32.160
<i>Shigeno's disposition gave us this motivation, by not running away from the game when it started raining.</i>

00:08:35.490 --> 00:08:37.550
Kokubu, give the message.

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:38.700
Y-Yes, sir!

00:08:45.860 --> 00:08:51.740
Kaido Academy High School's pitcher, Ichihara-kun, is being replaced by Akutsu-kun.

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:54.060
They're changing pitchers?

00:08:54.060 --> 00:08:55.130
Amazing!

00:08:55.130 --> 00:08:57.300
They knocked out the starting pitcher!

00:08:57.590 --> 00:08:58.750
Thanks for the work.

00:08:58.750 --> 00:09:00.700
Well, luck didn't seem to be with you,{Time check these two lines}

00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:04.180
but with these hideous results, we've got no choice.{Time check these two lines}

00:09:05.390 --> 00:09:08.890
You can get a taste of our victory on the bench at Koshien.

00:09:08.890 --> 00:09:09.810
Akutsu!

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:18.490
<i>I never imagined Ichihara would be switched out in the fifth inning...</i>

00:09:19.180 --> 00:09:21.220
<i>This is a bad turn of events.</i>

00:09:22.360 --> 00:09:26.210
Shigeno, what's that second pitcher like?

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:29.360
He's a knuckle-baller with a bad attitude.

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:30.460
"Knuckle-baller"?

00:09:31.310 --> 00:09:32.740
What's that?

00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:36.090
Well, watch and you'll find out.

00:09:36.360 --> 00:09:43.050
It's difficult even for me and Taiga to hit it our first at-bat.

00:09:43.050 --> 00:09:46.530
Batting fifth: second baseman, Fuji-kun.

00:09:47.180 --> 00:09:48.520
All right, bring it!

00:09:49.710 --> 00:09:51.280
He's completely into it!

00:09:51.560 --> 00:09:54.980
I'll teach you that you won't have any more luck...

00:09:54.980 --> 00:09:56.780
against me!

00:09:58.030 --> 00:09:58.950
<i>What!?</i>

00:10:00.290 --> 00:10:01.900
Strike!

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:03.710
He's useless.

00:10:03.710 --> 00:10:05.060
Is he really?

00:10:05.060 --> 00:10:06.370
He's definitely useless.

00:10:08.490 --> 00:10:12.370
You might've had a miracle when you got a hit off of Ichihara, but...

00:10:12.370 --> 00:10:15.130
your bat won't even touch my knuckle ball!

00:10:21.530 --> 00:10:26.510
This is a free fansub.

00:10:21.530 --> 00:10:26.510
Not for sale or rent.

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:28.680
He hit it!

00:10:28.680 --> 00:10:29.730
No way!

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:39.960
They did it!

00:10:39.960 --> 00:10:40.950
They're tied!

00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:44.560
How's that!?

00:10:45.190 --> 00:10:47.360
That pitch back there was a knuckle ball, right?

00:10:47.360 --> 00:10:49.750
How did he hit it so easily?

00:10:50.220 --> 00:10:51.680
I don't know.

00:10:51.680 --> 00:10:55.650
Maybe because Fuji's swings are so inconsistent,

00:10:55.650 --> 00:10:59.970
an unsteady pitch like the knuckle was hit right back with unsteadiness.

00:11:00.400 --> 00:11:02.750
In other words, it was a complete fluke.

00:11:02.750 --> 00:11:05.010
Well, that's one way to say it...

00:11:05.870 --> 00:11:07.120
What's with that?

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:11.020
But it's amazing that we've tied it, everyone.

00:11:11.550 --> 00:11:15.540
Luck is said to be another skill, so take pride in it.

00:11:17.340 --> 00:11:18.260
Strike!

00:11:18.260 --> 00:11:19.190
Batter out!

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:21.150
Three outs! Change!

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:24.860
All right! It starts now!

00:11:25.340 --> 00:11:26.360
Damn!

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:30.650
Don't get the wrong idea, you guys!

00:11:30.650 --> 00:11:33.830
That was just a once-in-a-blue-moon accident.

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:35.970
This is unsightly, Akutsu.

00:11:35.970 --> 00:11:38.750
Results are everything for us third-years.

00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:41.100
If they score runs, we'll just get them back.

00:11:42.350 --> 00:11:45.800
Stop making excuses and get to your at-bat already.

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:50.260
Bottom of the fifth inning: leading off for Kaido Academy...

00:11:50.540 --> 00:11:53.540
Batting ninth: pitcher, Akutsu-kun.

00:11:57.870 --> 00:12:01.530
<i>After this are the guys who go for my loose pitches at the top of the lineup.</i>

00:12:02.580 --> 00:12:05.210
<i>We've finally tied it.</i>

00:12:06.760 --> 00:12:10.410
<i>I'll never... let you score any more runs!</i>

00:12:11.730 --> 00:12:13.080
Strike!

00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:17.290
Strike two!

00:12:18.040 --> 00:12:19.050
Fast!

00:12:26.910 --> 00:12:27.880
Ball!

00:12:28.930 --> 00:12:30.140
Sorry, sorry!

00:12:35.940 --> 00:12:37.100
Ball!

00:12:38.810 --> 00:12:41.250
Well, that's strange!

00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:45.530
Maybe my legs are uncomfortable here like Ichihara's were!

00:12:53.840 --> 00:12:54.830
Dead ball!

00:12:56.260 --> 00:12:57.790
Dodge it, sucker.

00:12:58.070 --> 00:13:00.620
Hey, did you hear that!?

00:13:00.620 --> 00:13:03.830
He didn't even take his cap off! He told me to dodge it!

00:13:03.830 --> 00:13:05.640
Outrageous!

00:13:06.280 --> 00:13:07.300
T-Time!

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:11.690
Hey, what's going on all of a sudden?

00:13:12.150 --> 00:13:13.980
Saying that your footing's bad...

00:13:13.980 --> 00:13:16.310
They put more dirt on it, so...

00:13:18.140 --> 00:13:21.420
A-Are you saying the painkiller for your foot is...?

00:13:21.420 --> 00:13:22.370
Idiot.

00:13:22.370 --> 00:13:24.130
That's not it.

00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:29.030
I just don't want to jump into the piranha lake unarmed.

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:34.240
Batting first: center fielder, Kusano-kun.

00:13:45.830 --> 00:13:47.350
Strike!

00:13:51.580 --> 00:13:53.500
<i>"Piranha lake"?</i>

00:13:53.820 --> 00:13:58.260
<i>The first, third, and fourth batter are going after my weakness, the loose pitches.</i>

00:13:58.260 --> 00:14:04.980
<i>At this rate, if I face them directly, they'll just keep their mouths wide open and wait for their prey.</i>

00:14:05.590 --> 00:14:10.560
<i>But if that's how they're doing things, I have an idea.</i>

00:14:11.990 --> 00:14:14.340
<i>The prey that you're hunting for...</i>

00:14:14.340 --> 00:14:16.370
<i>I'll put poison in it!</i>

00:14:16.720 --> 00:14:17.530
<i>It's here!</i>

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:24.090
All right!

00:14:24.430 --> 00:14:25.840
<i>Crap!</i>

00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:28.630
<i>I threw a loose pitch before I closed in on him.</i>

00:14:29.210 --> 00:14:32.600
Batting second: second baseman, Tokashiki-kun.

00:14:36.340 --> 00:14:37.410
First!

00:14:39.040 --> 00:14:40.190
Out!

00:14:40.730 --> 00:14:44.190
Batting third: third baseman, Yakushiji-kun.

00:14:44.560 --> 00:14:47.990
One out with someone on second and third, and a clean-up hitter.

00:14:47.990 --> 00:14:48.990
Not good.

00:14:50.550 --> 00:14:54.450
You guys don't think you're seeing a weird dream, do you?

00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:58.450
It looks like the goddess of victory is on your side,

00:14:58.450 --> 00:14:59.420
but that doesn't matter to me.

00:15:01.490 --> 00:15:06.590
From the start, we've never relied on something like that.

00:15:08.940 --> 00:15:11.090
I'll bring you down no matter how many times it takes!

00:15:14.070 --> 00:15:15.560
<i>I'm counting on you.</i>

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:18.560
<i>Let me close in on them before I throw a loose pitch!</i>

00:15:22.850 --> 00:15:23.980
Strike!

00:15:29.480 --> 00:15:33.790
<i>While he closed in on Akutsu to start off, then put him on base by hitting him,</i>

00:15:35.360 --> 00:15:38.200
<i>to the normal eye, it was just a wild pitch, but...</i>

00:15:38.750 --> 00:15:42.000
<i>it clearly shows that Goro-kun is testing something.</i>

00:15:42.620 --> 00:15:44.950
<i>If I'm seeing things correctly...</i>

00:15:48.030 --> 00:15:49.720
Strike two!

00:15:50.120 --> 00:15:53.250
<i>Okay! I've really closed in on him this time.</i>

00:15:56.920 --> 00:15:58.590
<i>We're not just doing this for fun!</i>

00:15:58.590 --> 00:15:59.760
<i>Here I go, Tashiro!</i>

00:16:00.930 --> 00:16:02.310
<i>It's the loose pitch!</i>

00:16:05.770 --> 00:16:06.680
Strike!

00:16:06.680 --> 00:16:08.310
Batter out!

00:16:09.580 --> 00:16:13.570
Trying to get another hit with those sneaky hands? You have no shame.

00:16:13.830 --> 00:16:14.810
What!?

00:16:14.810 --> 00:16:17.040
He disguised it as a loose pitch when it was actually a forkball!?

00:16:17.470 --> 00:16:18.880
<i>As I thought.</i>

00:16:18.880 --> 00:16:23.430
<i>But do you think a forkball at that low level would work on me?</i>

00:16:23.900 --> 00:16:25.000
<i>Goro-kun...</i>

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:28.260
Batting fourth: catcher, Sato-kun.

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:31.910
<i>In the end, is that all you can do?</i>

00:16:31.910 --> 00:16:34.000
<i>You're getting rusty, Shigeno.</i>

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:45.120
<i>A forkball!?</i>

00:16:45.120 --> 00:16:46.270
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:16:46.270 --> 00:16:50.240
<i>Of course, I can't use it sharply and cleanly, but...</i>

00:16:50.750 --> 00:16:54.280
<i>They don't think I'll throw breaking balls,</i>

00:16:54.280 --> 00:16:57.990
<i>and if I disguise it as a loose pitch, they should swing at the air.</i>

00:17:01.110 --> 00:17:04.130
<i>But, is that good enough, Shigeno?</i>

00:17:05.450 --> 00:17:10.210
<i>I thought it was your ideal not to rely on breaking balls.</i>

00:17:10.730 --> 00:17:15.670
<i>If you start using the pretense of a forkball at this time, will you be okay with it?</i>

00:17:19.100 --> 00:17:20.450
<i>"Ideal"?</i>

00:17:21.360 --> 00:17:25.150
<i>That's fine. I just want to defeat Kaido, that's all.</i>

00:17:27.170 --> 00:17:28.370
<i>All right.</i>

00:17:28.370 --> 00:17:29.550
<i>A forkball, right?</i>

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:33.800
<i>Tashiro!</i>

00:17:36.240 --> 00:17:43.230
<i>My ideal right now is for Seishuu to win and go to Koshien.</i>

00:17:44.890 --> 00:17:49.680
<i>That's why I can't stand on the mound solely for my own pride.</i>

00:17:49.680 --> 00:17:51.200
Strike!

00:17:56.110 --> 00:17:57.510
Strike!

00:17:57.960 --> 00:18:00.570
<i>All right, I've closed in on Toshiya too.</i>

00:18:00.570 --> 00:18:03.320
<i>As long as I don't mess up my control...</i>

00:18:06.430 --> 00:18:07.220
<i>He fell for it!</i>

00:18:11.950 --> 00:18:13.810
Foul! Foul!

00:18:15.260 --> 00:18:16.820
That was close!

00:18:24.420 --> 00:18:26.450
<i>That was naive, Shigeno.</i>

00:18:26.450 --> 00:18:31.460
<i>Did you actually think that such a simple forkball would work on Sato?</i>

00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:36.070
S-Shigeno...

00:18:37.350 --> 00:18:38.510
Damn it!

00:18:41.980 --> 00:18:44.530
<i>Damn it... I don't have any way around him!</i>

00:18:44.530 --> 00:18:47.480
<i>At this rate, he'll get one of my loose pitches and end everything in one swing!</i>

00:18:48.810 --> 00:18:50.690
<i>I have to do something...</i>

00:18:51.340 --> 00:18:53.040
<i>I have to do something!</i>

00:18:53.500 --> 00:18:55.900
<i>Am I not the catcher!?</i>

00:18:58.680 --> 00:19:00.870
<i>Shigeno's on the edge.</i>

00:19:09.560 --> 00:19:10.700
Ball!

00:19:11.540 --> 00:19:12.670
<i>It's no use!</i>

00:19:12.670 --> 00:19:14.590
<i>We should just give him first base.</i>

00:19:14.590 --> 00:19:17.460
<i>But Shigeno isn't the type to listen to that...</i>

00:19:20.840 --> 00:19:22.510
W-What!?

00:19:22.880 --> 00:19:23.790
An intentional walk?

00:19:23.790 --> 00:19:24.640
Him?

00:19:26.750 --> 00:19:30.930
<i>He was throwing breaking balls to win.</i>

00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:35.270
<i>If we walk the fourth batter, Sato,</i>

00:19:35.270 --> 00:19:37.320
<i>there won't be any problems.</i>

00:19:44.570 --> 00:19:45.660
Ball!

00:19:46.380 --> 00:19:48.340
You just do as you're told.

00:19:49.420 --> 00:19:53.290
Doing trick plays, letting him throw weak forkballs...

00:19:54.410 --> 00:19:58.500
If I were his catcher, I would never let him do those kinds of things.

00:19:59.900 --> 00:20:02.260
Nothing seemed to work, so you'll just walk me?

00:20:02.990 --> 00:20:04.430
That's great for me.

00:20:04.430 --> 00:20:06.860
If your pitcher is so ready to run away,

00:20:06.860 --> 00:20:09.580
knocking him out is only a matter of time.

00:20:17.430 --> 00:20:19.650
T-Time, please!

00:20:22.630 --> 00:20:24.270
Let's face him, Shigeno!

00:20:24.270 --> 00:20:24.910
What!?

00:20:25.260 --> 00:20:27.110
Don't run away, Shigeno!

00:20:27.110 --> 00:20:29.580
That's not like you!

00:20:29.580 --> 00:20:34.430
With just probabilities and petty tricks, we won't be able to defeat Kaido!

00:20:36.300 --> 00:20:38.810
If there's any chance for us to win,

00:20:38.810 --> 00:20:43.550
it'll be with fastballs embedded with your spirit in a direct challenge!

00:20:48.420 --> 00:20:50.580
What are you trying to do, looking all cool like that!?

00:20:50.580 --> 00:20:55.310
He can cut the fastballs and then hit a loose pitch in the end!

00:20:55.640 --> 00:20:59.270
But he's <i>only</i> cutting them.

00:20:59.650 --> 00:21:03.500
He hasn't truly hit your gyroball!

00:21:03.500 --> 00:21:04.680
That's right!

00:21:04.680 --> 00:21:08.290
He's not <i>just</i> cutting them, cutting them is all he can do!

00:21:08.610 --> 00:21:12.960
Yeah, and if he hits one of the loose pitches, that's fine with us.

00:21:14.640 --> 00:21:16.210
This isn't like you.

00:21:16.210 --> 00:21:18.090
Pitch the way you like to!

00:21:18.090 --> 00:21:21.210
No one will complain if we lose like that.

00:21:31.730 --> 00:21:32.430
Play!

00:21:34.190 --> 00:21:38.150
<i>I didn't think they'd seriously be provoked by me.</i>

00:21:54.290 --> 00:21:55.950
<i>Bring it, Shigeno!</i>

00:22:02.390 --> 00:22:04.000
Foul!

00:22:08.750 --> 00:22:09.510
Foul!

00:22:10.590 --> 00:22:11.670
Foul!

00:22:13.000 --> 00:22:14.030
<i>This is weird.</i>

00:22:14.030 --> 00:22:15.470
<i>How many pitches has it been?</i>

00:22:16.080 --> 00:22:18.550
<i>A loose pitch should've come by now.</i>

00:22:22.970 --> 00:22:24.710
<i>The speed of this ball...</i>

00:22:25.750 --> 00:22:26.530
Foul!

00:22:29.160 --> 00:22:30.490
Thank you.

00:22:31.950 --> 00:22:34.440
My eyes were opened by your advice.

00:22:34.930 --> 00:22:37.480
It reminded me that this is all we have.

00:22:51.880 --> 00:22:52.760
Strike!

00:22:52.760 --> 00:22:53.970
Batter out!

00:22:53.970 --> 00:22:55.220
He did it!

00:22:55.670 --> 00:22:56.680
All right!

00:22:59.300 --> 00:23:01.580
<i>That's how it should be, Shigeno.</i>

00:23:03.410 --> 00:23:06.610
<i>It's finally become an interesting game.</i>

00:24:40.530 --> 00:24:42.750
It stays tied through to the eighth inning.

00:24:42.750 --> 00:24:45.590
The painkiller for my foot has finally begun to wear off.

00:24:45.590 --> 00:24:48.640
Kaido starts to waver from Egashira's ballistic orders.

00:24:48.640 --> 00:24:51.880
Which way will the flow of the game swing?

00:24:52.890 --> 00:24:54.160
Next time, on Major:

00:24:54.160 --> 00:24:55.180
A Close Battle.

00:24:55.790 --> 00:24:58.030
Run to the stage of your dreams!
